.TH sam-jail-group 1 2026-11-23 "SAM 0.1.0" "SAM - Sandboxed AppImage Manager"
.SH NAME
sam\-jail\-group \- Change permissions of several sandboxed apps at once
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsam\-jail group\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change permissions of several sandboxed apps at once
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sam\-jail\-group\-list(1)
Every sandboxed app with its permissions and permission tags
.TP
sam\-jail\-group\-set(1)
Set one permission to the same value for several apps. Prints the settings from before as "previous", for `group restore`
.TP
sam\-jail\-group\-restore(1)
Undo a `group set`: reads the "undo" object it printed (JSON on stdin) and takes back only that change
